{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092883-artifacts-and-reach","id":1092883,"title":"Artifacts and Reach","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-15T11:26:25-07:00","id":1092883,"title":"Artifacts and Reach","content":"The rules on this are vague (or rather, non-existent). When you map spell effects for Artifacts, does that include their Reach effects? The merit says &quot;Artifacts cannot Reach beyond the 'free' Reach for their Arcana ratings on their own. If an Artifact risks Paradox, the user can spend Mana to mitigate Paradox (in any combination of her own or the Artifact\u2019s Mana pool, up to her Gnosis-derived limits) and may choose to contain the Paradox herself. Otherwise, the Artifact automatically releases it.&quot; This implies that mages can alter the effects that the Artifact casts with their own Reach? Is this limited to only some Artifacts, or can all do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T13:34:12-07:00","id":1092933,"title":"","content":"Either or both because that specific question would be answered by the ST. Personally, I assume that artifacts have triggers which can activate their powers automatically, and these effects never go over their free Reach. Mages however can override this restriction when they activate an artifact and force it to use more Reach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:23:32-07:00","id":1092980,"title":"","content":"That's a fairly sane way to interpret it. For me it personally depends on the artifact. Some allow mages to alter their Reach, others don't.<br /> <br /> Does one need to apply Instant Casting to an artifact's power, or do the trigger conditions override that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T16:34:35-07:00","id":1093010,"title":"","content":"There's no guidance, so I'd personally let a Mage push an Artifact beyond its Free Reach if he wanted. Paradox makes the world (and the game) go round, after all.<br /> <br /> Also yes, you need to apply Reach to get Instant Casting for an Artifact, which means many Artifacts will only have that option for their lesser effects.<br /> However there's no reason for you to &quot;have&quot; to do that.<br /> In my last game we had an Artifact called the &quot;Reliquary of Animation&quot; containing the Golem spell.<br /> It took a scene to activate without Mage assistance, but given that it was extra spell control, the players were very happy to deal with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T16:35:10-07:00","id":1093011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092883-artifacts-and-reach?p=1092980#post1092980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fairly sane way to interpret it. For me it personally depends on the artifact. Some allow mages to alter their Reach, others don't.<br /> <br /> Does one need to apply Instant Casting to an artifact's power, or do the trigger conditions override that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I would assume it can go either way, although those two options aren't actually mutually exclusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T16:46:56-07:00","id":1093018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Artifacts cannot Reach beyond the 'free' Reach for their Arcana ratings on their own. If an Artifact risks Paradox, the user can spend Mana to mitigate Paradox (in any combination of her own or the Artifact\u2019s Mana pool, up to her Gnosis-derived limits) and may choose to contain the Paradox herself. Otherwise, the Artifact automatically releases it </div> </div> </div>I always thought that an Artifact risking Paradox, despite being limited to free Reach, was under the assumption that the wielder uses it in front of Sleepers. Or that the mage using it has already risked Paradox with his spells in that scene, and trying to use the Artifact in the same scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:42:04-07:00","id":1093213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092883-artifacts-and-reach?p=1093018#post1093018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always thought that an Artifact risking Paradox, despite being limited to free Reach, was under the assumption that the wielder uses it in front of Sleepers. Or that the mage using it has already risked Paradox with his spells in that scene, and trying to use the Artifact in the same scene.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's this one.<br /> <br /> Artifacts have the Reach effects for their spells built in, the way Attainments do - and can't exceed that given by their Arcanum rating. They can risk Paradox by casting an obvious spell in front of a Sleeper, or other means of gaining Paradox dice on a spell, but automatically release it unless the weilder chooses to spend Mana to buy it down and/or Contain it in herself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:51:41-07:00","id":1093218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1092883-artifacts-and-reach?p=1093213#post1093213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's this one.<br /> <br /> Artifacts have the Reach effects for their spells built in, the way Attainments do - and can't exceed that given by their Arcanum rating. They can risk Paradox by casting an obvious spell in front of a Sleeper, or other means of gaining Paradox dice on a spell, but automatically release it unless the weilder chooses to spend Mana to buy it down and/or Contain it in herself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you for the clarification. I think it's the &quot;on their own&quot; part that was confusing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T15:19:43-07:00","id":1093428,"title":"","content":"Well, it also covers what happens with those Sleepwalkers with Relic Attuned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}